{"id":55,"number":35,"symbol":"Nak","name":"Sodium/potassium-transporting ATPase α1","gene":"ATP1A1","family":"TRN","location":"P","other_locations":[],"cell_rank":0,"mass_kda":112.9,"length_aa":1023,"discovery_year":1957,"milestone":"Na⁺/K⁺-ATPase discovered (Skou, Nobel 1997)","blurb":"Pumps 3 Na⁺ out and 2 K⁺ in; uses about a fifth of your energy at rest.","drugs":["Digoxin"],"therapeutic":null,"pathways":[],"orthologs":{"ecoli":null,"human":"ATP1A1","mouse":"Atp1a1"},"variant_count":0,"misfolded":null,"uniprot_id":"P05023","function":"Catalytic subunit of the Na(+)/K(+)-ATPase pump that hydrolyzes ATP to exchange ions across the plasma membrane, exporting 3 Na(+) and importing 2 K(+) per cycle against electrochemical gradients. It undergoes ATP-driven conformational changes that allow alternating binding and release of Na(+) and K(+) ions across the membrane. This process maintains essential Na(+) and K(+) gradients for membrane potential and cellular function. Could also be part of an osmosensory signaling pathway that senses body-fluid sodium levels and controls salt intake behavior as well as voluntary water intake to regulate sodium homeostasis","sequence":"","pdb_ids":["7E20","7E21","9KCI","9KCK","9KCL","9KCM","9KCG","9KCJ","7E1Z","9KCR"],"alphafold_url":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-P05023-F1-model_v6.pdb","variants":[],"partners":[{"id":91,"symbol":"Kras","name":"GTPase KRas","score":0.813,"effect_out":null,"effect_in":null},{"id":127,"symbol":"Tau","name":"Microtubule-associated protein tau","score":0.802,"effect_out":null,"effect_in":null}]}